The error is caused by this line:

const accounts = getDB.find({}).toArray;

You're assigning the toArray function itself, not calling it. Then Express tries to send a function:

res.send(accounts); // accounts is a function

res.send() internally calls Buffer.from() for some values, which is why you get:

TypeError [ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE]
Received function toArray
Fix

Call toArray() with parentheses and await it:

app.get("/allAcounts", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    await client.connect();

    const collection = client.db("allAcounts").collection("acounts");
    const accounts = await collection.find({}).toArray();

    res.status(200).send(accounts);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
    res.status(500).send({
      error: "Could not get all accounts",
      value: error.message,
    });
  } finally {
    await client.close();
  }
});
There's another bug

In your finally block you have:

await client.close;

This also isn't calling the function. It should be:

await client.close();
One more recommendation

It's generally not recommended to connect and close MongoDB for every request. Instead:

await client.connect(); // once when the server starts

app.get("/allAcounts", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const accounts = await client
      .db("allAcounts")
      .collection("acounts")
      .find({})
      .toArray();

    res.json(accounts);
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
});

This reuses the same MongoDB connection, which is the standard approach with the MongoDB Node.js driver.

